# PL-300 Objectives Checklist

This checklist is based on the main skills measured in the PL-300 exam.  
Use it to track what you’ve really *mastered*, not just watched once 😉

---

## Overall Progress

- [X] I can load data into Power BI and clean it on my own
- [X] I can build a proper data model with relationships and DAX measures
- [X] I can create clear, interactive reports that answer business questions
- [ ] I understand the basics of Power BI Service, sharing, and security
- [ ] I feel ready to do a full practice exam without looking things up

---

## Project milestones & timing

Use these milestones to decide **when** to build (or upgrade) a project.  
Rough idea: after 1–2 study sessions on a topic → do a small project.

- [X] **Mini Project 1 – Data Cleaning**
  - Target timing: after you’ve done basic *Prepare the data* modules.
  - Build a small report from a single Excel/CSV source.
  - Use Power Query to clean data (remove columns, fix data types, filter rows).

- [X] **Project 2 – Sales Model v1**
  - Target timing: after you’ve learned basic relationships and simple DAX.
  - Create a model with multiple tables (e.g. Sales, Customers, Products).
  - Add basic measures (`SUM`, `COUNT`, simple `CALCULATE`) and a few core visuals.

- [ ] **Project 3 – Sales Dashboard v2 (Insights)**
  - Target timing: after you’ve covered *Visualize & analyze the data* basics.
  - Take Project 2 and upgrade it:
    - Add slicers, drillthrough, tooltips, cards/KPIs.
    - Focus on answering concrete questions (best month, best customer, etc.).

- [ ] **Project 4 – Alternative Scenario Report**
  - Target timing: after you’re comfortable with several visuals and filters.
  - Use a different dataset (customers, marketing, operations… anything).
  - Focus on variety: matrix, line charts, conditional formatting, sorting, etc.

- [ ] **Project 5 – Published Report with RLS**
  - Target timing: after you’ve studied *Manage & secure Power BI*.
  - Publish one of your existing projects to Power BI Service.
  - Set up Row-Level Security (RLS) and test with “View as role”.

